            "ending.declarative_contrast"
          ],
          "source": "80325",
          "reason": "The plain present connective has consonant versus vowel/rieul verb attachment and only honorific prefinal attachment. A vowel/rieul owner cannot take literal -는다; a consonant-final ㅂ stem cannot use -ㄴ다 through vowel-boundary restoration, and past/modal prefinals take plain -다 instead. This judgment excludes only the represented whole-connective path."
